<title>USA: MSB Financial buys back five pct of stock.</title>
<headline>MSB Financial buys back five pct of stock.</headline>
<dateline>MARSHALL, Mich. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>MSB Financial Inc, a holding company for Marshall Savings Bank FSB, said Wednesday it has completed the repurchase of 33,790 shares, or five percent, of its common stock.</p>
<p>The total cost of the repurchase was $598,000 or an average price of $17.70 per share.</p>
<p>Upon completion of this repurchase program, MSB Financial has 642,014 shares of common stock outstanding.</p>
<p>Marshall Savings Bank has two offices in Marshall, Mich., and specializes in residential mortgage lending and retail banking services. On September 30, 1996, the company's assets totaled $62.8 million.</p>
<p>	  ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
